'''Expansión''' ({{Literal translation|expansion}}; {{Langx|mxi|إِسْبَانْسِيُونْ|Isbansiyun}}) is a [[Boroughs of Castejón|borough]] of the [[Castejón|Metropolitan City of Castejón]]. It is the fourth largest borough geographically, and is adjacent to the boroughs of  [[Sástago]] (north) and [[Ampurias]] (southeast). It is bounded to the north by [[Oñoico Bay]] (itself an extension of the larger [[Salto Bay]]), and the south by the [[Alagón River|Alagón river]]. It is the fourth most populous borough, with a population of 2,736,507 residents in 2025, approximately 26.7 percent of them foreign-born.  

Expansión was blocked from further expansion with the creation of the [[Sástago]] borough in 1896.

The borough is primarily {{W|residential}}, with a mix of tenements, {{W|apartment blocks}}, {{W|housing cooperatives}}, {{W|townhouses}}, and renovated {{W|rowhouses}}, but its many retail businesses reflect the ethnic and social diversity of the population. The area has a large LGBTQ population, concentrated in and around [[Papallona]]. About one-eighth of Expansión area is open space, and it includes several famous monuments, such as the [[Arco de Humanidad|''Arco de Humanidad'']]. Expansión's open spaces are situated primarily on land deliberately reserved in the late 19th century as urban development progressed to the northwest from [[Ampurias]] (see [[Commissioners Plan of 1881]]). 

Due to the {{W|verticalization}} and {{W|gentrification}} of Expansión's waterfronts there was a widening {{W|income gap}} between the wealthier living in luxury high-rise buildings and less-wealthy individuals. This led to tension within the community with [[Sant Dídac#Rioting during 2021 unrest|2021 Sant Dídac riots]], resulting in measures to address and reverse growing inequality. 

